---
/**
 * /about/ (WEB-FEAT-035, SEO_PLAYBOOK.md §14): who makes PalmSays and why, how the scanner
 * and the AI work in plain words, the limits, company details, contact and the grievance
 * contact (DPDP). Facts only from the repo docs and the app (CONTENT_GUIDE.md §4.8, §9.1):
 * no invented numbers, awards, reviews or credentials. English only (no reviewed Hindi twin).
 * Company details: owner item 9 (placeholders on a preview build; production refuses to build).
 */
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import DocPage from '../../components/trust/DocPage.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../config/site';
import { companyForBuild } from '../../lib/legal-page';
import { ORGANIZATION_ID, PERSON_ID, WEBSITE_ID, organizationSchema } from '../../lib/schema';

const company = companyForBuild();
const path = '/about/';
const brand = site.brand;
const authorPath = '/about/deepak-chauhan/';
const personId = PERSON_ID;

const toc = [
  { id: 'what', label: 'What PalmSays is' },
  { id: 'how', label: 'How a reading works' },
  { id: 'limits', label: 'What it can’t do' },
  { id: 'who', label: 'Who makes it' },
  { id: 'money', label: 'How we make money' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Company and contact' },
];

const steps = [
  { title: 'The photo is checked on your phone', body: 'Light, sharpness and a whole palm in the frame. A photo that won’t work is caught before anything is sent.' },
  { title: 'The lines are traced', body: 'Our line scanner, running on Modal in the USA, traces the heart, head, life and fate lines it can see on your own photo.' },
  { title: 'The palm is described in words', body: 'Cloudflare Workers AI writes down what it sees, for example “heart line: long, curved”. Neither service keeps the photo.' },
  { title: 'Meanings come from the books', body: 'A fixed rule set built from classical palmistry books matches what was seen to meanings. Every meaning keeps the book and chapter it comes from.' },
  { title: 'The report is written', body: 'An AI language model writes the report in plain words from those observations and the matched meanings. It never sees the photo, and a filter checks every sentence for claims we never make.' },
];

const organization = {
  ...organizationSchema(),
  founder: { '@id': personId },
  ...(site.company.email ? { email: site.company.email } : {}),
  ...(site.company.name ? { legalName: site.company.name } : {}),
};
const aboutPage = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  '@id': `${site.baseUrl}${path}#webpage`,
  name: `About ${brand}`,
  url: `${site.baseUrl}${path}`,
  inLanguage: 'en',
  isPartOf: { '@id': WEBSITE_ID },
  mainEntity: { '@id': ORGANIZATION_ID },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About ${brand}: who we are and how it works`}
  description={`${brand} traces the lines on a photo of your own palm and explains them from classical palmistry books, with the limits said plainly. Who makes it and how.`}
  path={path}
  locale="en"
  jsonLd={[aboutPage, organization]}
>
  <DocPage
    crumb="About"
    path={path}
    icon="palm-lines"
    kicker="About us"
    title={`About ${brand}`}
    lead={`${brand} reads the lines on a photo of your own palm and explains them the way the classical palmistry books do, with the source of every meaning and the limits said plainly.`}
    meta={`Made in India. Operated by ${company.name}.`}
    toc={toc}
  >
    <h2 id="what">What {brand} is</h2>
    <p>
      {brand} is an Android app and this website. You take a photo of your palm; we trace the major lines on that photo and show what
      traditional Indian palmistry (Hast Rekha Shastra) and the classical books say about them, in English and Hindi.
    </p>
    <p>
      We built it because a palm reading should be about your own hand. {brand} shows your own lines on your own photo, says where each
      meaning comes from, and says so when a line isn’t clear in the photo.
    </p>
    <p>
      {
        site.webReadingEnabled
          ? 'You can take a reading on this website or in the Android app.'
          : 'Today the full reading is in the Android app; the reading on this website opens later. The guides and the photo tools here are free to use now.'
      }
    </p>

    <h2 id="how">How a reading works</h2>
    <ol class="about-steps">
      {
        steps.map((step, index) => (
          <li class="about-step">
            <span class="about-step-num" aria-hidden="true">{index + 1}</span>
            <span class="about-step-copy">
              <strong>{step.title}</strong>
              <span>{step.body}</span>
            </span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
    <p>
      The photo tools on this website are simpler: a hand model runs on your own phone or computer to measure your hand shape and
      fingers, and the photo never leaves your device. The full details of what is stored, and for how long, are in the <a class="text-link" href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="limits">What it can’t do</h2>
    <ul class="doc-points">
      <li class="doc-point"><Icon name="info" class="doc-point-icon" /><span>Palmistry is a tradition for reflection, not a science. Palm lines can’t tell dates, how long you’ll live, your health, whether or when you’ll marry, how many children you’ll have, or how much money you’ll make. {brand} never tells you these.</span></li>
      <li class="doc-point"><Icon name="camera" class="doc-point-icon" /><span>A photo can hide things. Light, a crease or the crop can make a line look broken or short, and small marks such as islands, stars and crosses are too small for most phone cameras, so we leave them out of reports.</span></li>
      <li class="doc-point"><Icon name="book" class="doc-point-icon" /><span>The books don’t always agree. Where they read a feature in different ways, we show both instead of quietly picking one.</span></li>
      <li class="doc-point"><Icon name="tick" class="doc-point-icon" /><span>Readings are for people aged {site.ageRule} and over, and never replace a doctor, a lawyer or a financial adviser.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p>More in <a class="text-link" href="/is-palmistry-real/">Is palmistry true?</a> and in our <a class="text-link" href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="who">Who makes it</h2>
    <p>
      {brand} is made in India by its founder, <a class="text-link" href={authorPath}>{site.author.name}</a>. He builds the app and this website and writes the guides from the
      classical books listed in our <a class="text-link" href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>. He is not a professional palm
      reader, and we don’t claim to be: the meanings come from the books, each with its source.
    </p>

    <h2 id="money">How we make money</h2>
    <p>
      The Android app sells reading packs and monthly or yearly plans through Google Play; prices are on the <a class="text-link" href="/app/">app page</a>. There are no ads, we don’t sell your data, and we sell no gems, pujas or remedies.
      The guides and tools link to the app, and that is our interest in them.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">Company and contact</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Operator:</strong> {company.name}</li>
      <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a class="text-link" href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a></li>
      <li><strong>Grievance contact</strong> (questions about your data, India’s DPDP Act): {company.grievanceContact}</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">We answer within 30 days. To delete your account, use the <a class="text-link" href="/delete-account/">delete-account page</a>.</p>
  </DocPage>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-steps { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; display: grid; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .about-step {
    display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: flex-start; max-width: none; padding: 1rem 1.125rem; border-radius: var(--r-well); border: 1px solid transparent;
    background: var(--well) padding-box, var(--rim) border-box; box-shadow: var(--shine);
  }
  .about-step-num {
    display: inline-grid; place-items: center; flex: none; width: 2.25rem; height: 2.25rem; border-radius: 9999px;
    font-family: var(--ff-display); font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-on-gold); background-image: var(--gold-gradient);
  }
  .about-step-copy { display: grid; gap: 0.25rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .about-step-copy span { color: var(--fg-muted); }
</style>
